      <div>
        <div class="kicker">The problem</div>
        <h2>Traditional commercial real estate search starts too late.</h2>
      </div>
      <p>
        Most search experiences begin with available properties. That can be useful, but it often skips the harder question: which locations actually fit the business? A company may compare office districts, industrial corridors, customer access, commute patterns, and nearby alternatives before a single building makes sense.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="product-story__section product-story__section--split">
      <div>
        <div class="kicker">Why Rofo was created</div>
        <h2>To make commercial real estate easier to reason about.</h2>
      </div>
      <p>
        Rofo began as a commercial real estate listings site. Over time, the product has moved toward a broader view of commercial geography: cities, districts, corridors, representative buildings, market comparisons, and recommendations. The point is not to replace expert judgment. It is to help a business ask better questions before the live market investigation begins.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="product-story__section">
