      <div class="product-card-grid">
        <article>
          <h3>Clarity before volume</h3>
          <p>A smaller set of well-explained options is more useful than thousands of disconnected results.</p>
        </article>
        <article>
          <h3>Location context matters</h3>
          <p>Markets, districts, commute patterns, buildings, and alternatives all shape the quality of a decision.</p>
        </article>
        <article>
          <h3>Respect the user's time</h3>
          <p>Fast pages, clear language, and direct next steps matter when a business is trying to make a real decision.</p>
        </article>
        <article>
          <h3>Be honest about uncertainty</h3>
          <p>Recommendations can identify strong starting points. Live availability, pricing, and incentives still require market investigation.</p>
        </article>
